    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d46">

                <pb facs="0178" n="60" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg60"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">467n.11/11: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Jerusalem</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Jerusalem</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-10-18T14:00:00+02:00">October 18, 1929—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 18—9:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Inasmuch as the local law does not seem to afford adequate damages for injuries
                    and loss of life suffered during the recent disturbances <pb facs="0179" n="61"
                        xml:id="pg61"/> and since the character of the disturbances and other
                    elements involved therein might justify international claims, will the
                    Department please instruct me by telegraph whether I should make reservations in
                    this respect to the Palestine Government before the expiration of the 2 months’
                    limit?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knabenshue</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
